+# lose.dem — Story 1.4: the thinnest LOSE (the Error 404 stub). The 1.2 fixture;
+# draw only the FIRST leg (residential(0) → router(1)) — the sink is unreachable.
+# Spawn residential(0) → content_host(2): the packet flows to the router (t43)
+# then has no route onward + waits there (per-hop forwarding, E29). The run
+# reaches the tick cap (lose cap 3000ms = tick 60) with score 0 < goal 1 →
+# Run_Lost (terminal). The capture at 3000ms pins the terminal/lose frame (T1
+# hash carries outcome=Lost+Run_Lost; T2 pixel the stuck packet at the router).
+# run 3200ms lets a few post-terminal ticks exercise the barrier.
+seed 42
+run 3200ms
+at 500ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 2050ms spawn 0 2
+win goal 1
+lose cap 3000ms
+capture at 3000ms
+expect hash stable
